      "id": "key-text",
      "shape": "text",
      "role": "label",
      "face": "body",
      "text": "Blue: sequential actions. Grey: stop and recover manually.\nA failure stops at its own step. Later actions do not run.\nEach guard covers the actions since the previous decision.\nGrey exits show recovery points. The chapter table also covers evidence and promotion.\nCHANNEL selects ravel@2 or ravel through build, tap and installation.\nPromotion is separate from the version cut and needs no new archives.\nThe book build stays local. The Pages branch push precedes the tap.\nAfter a version write, keep that version. Do not start another version cut.\nA source/tag mismatch needs a decision. Never move a public tag.\nTask removes its lock on exit. After an abrupt stop, check for a live task first.",
